  "worked_solution": "To find the image of $F$ under the action of $T$, we first create a column-vector $x$ containing the coordinates of $F:$\n\n$$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $x$ under the action of $T$ by calculating the matrix product $Tx:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Tx & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 \\\\ 4 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe result, $Tx,$ contains the coordinates of ${F}^{\u2032}.$ Therefore, ${F}^{\u2032}(2,6).$",
